{
  "summary": "Require exact witness transaction ID (wtxid) matches when removing mempool transactions for a newly connected block. When a transaction in a block matches an entry in the local mempool by txid but differs in witness data, the local entry is removed with MemPoolRemovalReason::CONFLICT instead of BLOCK and excluded from the mined transactions list. In the mempool fee estimator, block coverage is calculated using mined transaction weights in a single pass over block data.",
  "problem": "CTxMemPool::removeForBlock previously matched transactions only by txid, which does not commit to witness data. If a transaction with the same txid but a different witness was mined, the local mempool variant was reported as mined, skewing the mempool fee estimator's health checks, causing the block policy estimator to record a confirmation for an unmined feerate bucket, and failing to emit conflict notifications to wallets and ZMQ subscribers.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The mempool estimator added in #34075 checks health by comparing the weight of mempool transactions removed for a block with the block’s non-coinbase transaction weight... A matched entry can therefore have a different weight from the mined transaction, skewing the coverage check. The block policy estimator also treats the local variant as confirmed even though its wtxid was not in the block.'",
    "Commit 777393c100 notes that removing the variant as CONFLICT drops it from fee tracking and notifies wallet and ZMQ subscribers with a removal event for the unmined variant."
  ],
